; iter-129 — EmberParticles bottom spray REMOVED. Pre-iter-129 the
; emitter painted 70 particles at scale 0.05-0.12 rising from a 4-px
; strip at y=760. Playtester read: "tiny random spray that adds
; almost nothing — leftover effect rather than deliberate atmosphere."
; Diagnosis: the emitter wasn't tied to any scene anchor. The two
; torch-ember emitters (Left/RightTorchEmbers) sit at the painted
; torch flames in the backdrop — they read as embers FROM the
; torches. The MistParticles emitter sits at the stair-mist line —
; reads as mist FROM the stairs. EmberParticles had no anchor — it
; just drifted up from a generic baseline.
;
; Following the user's design rule ("If a good ambient particle
; implementation cannot be done cleanly, it is better to have no
; particle effect at all than a weak one"), the emitter is retired
; rather than reworked. The torch + mist emitters carry all the
; ambient motion the screen needs.

; iter-92: Left torch ember emitter. Backdrop's left torch flame sits
; at roughly (495, 365) in the 1280×720 viewport (when the painting is
; covered-cropped). Small emitter sells the painted flame as alive.
;
; iter-130 retune — Dark Souls-pacing pass. Pre-iter-130 values
; (22 amount, 22-46 px/s velocity, 1.6s lifetime, 0.6-1.4 damping)
; read as "cinder spitter" rather than "lazy ember." Genre peers use
; sparse, slow embers that drift up several seconds before fading.
; Iter-130 values:
;   amount 22 → 14 (sparser = more deliberate)
;   initial_velocity 22-46 → 10-24 (half-speed; lazy drift, not zip)
;   lifetime 1.6 → 3.2s (doubled; embers linger long enough to read)
;   damping 0.6-1.4 → 0.3-0.7 (less friction = velocity holds, less
;     "abrupt stop and fade" feel)
;   scale 0.06-0.10 → 0.08-0.14 (slightly larger so the sparser
;     emitter still reads at a glance)
;   tangential_accel ±10 → ±5 (gentler swirl, less jitter)
[node name="LeftTorchEmbers" type="CPUParticles2D" parent="."]
